      "message": "fix(motion): adaptive growth overload fallback compares whole revolutions\n\nWhere no growth step holds the load, the step search kept the least\noverload from readings cut short at the first point past the bound.\nWhere the overload does not grow with the step, every try read the same,\nthe largest step won the tie and was walked whole far past the reading\nit was chosen on (island NE corner, #7 round 10: 59.5 deg chosen,\n125 deg cut).\n\nThe tried revolutions are now walked whole again from the planner's\nstock (least_whole), largest first; a smaller step replaces the kept one\nonly when it reads more than 2 % less, and each re-walk is abandoned once\nit can no longer win. The re-walks rebuild no geometry and re-read only\nrevolutions whose whole length the trial already charged, so the #13\ngrowth budget (WORK_MAX, GEOM_MAX/GEOM_LEN) is unchanged\n(docs/decisions/845-adaptive-overload-fallback.md).\n\nPinned by grow::tests::the_overload_fallback_keeps_the_least_whole_reading_not_a_truncated_tie.\n\nFixes #845\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R73FNJd8WUSV4o9J6yG2vG",
